picks the PYRON cell (id 0x11), which this build does not back (huitzil-m2
backs only Huitzil at 0x10). The exact twin of this set's own 11_pick_donovan
skip. The tenant pick on this build is covered by 37_pick_huitzil_cell; the
replay itself is NOT dead — pyron-m2 carries a real .sha1 for it.

Added 14z-78 (maintainer sign-off). The replay landed in 14z-75, after this
set was frozen (as huitzil-m1) in 14z-73, so the set had no entry for it and
the suite went red on an unaccounted replay — zero divergences throughout.
Found by the coverage matrix built while fixing the same gap on donovan-m3a:
the defect was never Donovan-specific, it is what happens to any frozen set
when the suite grows a replay for a tenant that set does not back.

NB: keep skip-reason prose free of the literal tokens a log scan greps for
(the verdict words). The first version of these three files contained them and
made a grep over the suite log report phantom failures.
